<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan money, bond markets close for holiday.</title>
<headline>Taiwan money, bond markets close for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's money and bond markets were closed on Thursday for public holiday. They will reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the overnight interbank rate closed at 5.856 percent against Tuesday's 6.081 close, with 30-day commercial paper falling to 6.10 percent against 6.25-6.30.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
</text>
